 ],
 "title": "Everything You Always Wanted to Know About Mathematics (But Didn\u2019t Even Know to Ask)",
 "byline": "Brendan W. Sullivan, with John Mackey \u00b7 Carnegie Mellon University, 2013 (thesis-book for CMU\u2019s Concepts of Mathematics)",
 "note": "Chapter introductions, summaries, exercises, \u201clookahead\u201d sections and the closing list of definitions and theorems are not broken out. Your Drive has three identical copies of this PDF; links go to one. Summaries are in our own words; the text stays in the PDF.",
 "summary": "A conversational, guided introduction to abstract mathematics and proof-writing written for CMU\u2019s first-year course. Part I teaches how to think mathematically: what mathematics and proof are, induction informally and then rigorously, sets, and logic with quantifiers and negation. Part II applies this to core topics: relations, orders and equivalence relations with modular arithmetic, functions and cardinality, and combinatorics (counting principles, double counting, selections with repetition, pigeonhole and inclusion\u2013exclusion)."
}